window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Princess Snow and Prince Henri couldn't be more different.</b></p> <p><b>Their kingdoms and families have been at enmity for a millennium.</b></p> <p><b>But when a new dark queen rises, they have little choice but to join forces.</b></p> <p>Princess Snow has been sheltered since birth, raised in a secret garden at her terrified father's behest. But when her father dies, and her brother grants Snow's freedom, life seems ready to finally begin... just in time for her brother's new wife to reveal a heart of jealousy and fear. Barely escaping the castle alive, Snow stumbles upon a group of kind-hearted mountain men—and the aggravatingly handsome prince who claims her brother asked him to find her.</p> <p>Crown Prince Henri Fortier of Destin had no intentions of journeying into the heart of his enemy's land. But when the newly crowned king of Tumen begs for help to find his missing sister, Henri goes in hopes of making peace. What he finds, however, is not what he expected.</p> <p>The princess is indeed alive, but she won't remain so if the king's new wife has her way. And with the new queen's blossoming powers, Henri knows he must intervene, not only for the princess, but for the entire realm. Helping would be much easier, however, if the princess didn't resent him so much. Which makes it even more confusing when he finds himself drawn to her—and wonders whether she's secretly drawn to him as well.</p> <p>None of that will matter, however, if the evil queen has her way. Can the two unlikely allies can't stop her? Or will a shadow of oppression will overtake everyone they love?</p> <p><i>For the magic of Narnia and the romance of fairy tales, listen today to escape into the Classical Kingdoms Collection, a series of clean fantasy fairy tale retellings with magical mystery, clean romance, and happily-ever-afters.</i></p> <p><b><i>Author's Note: The Huntsman's Heart features the same royal family from Beauty Beheld but can be listened to as a standalone novel.</i></b></p>"; 
